-#
  Pipeline automation kill switches (phase 10, DataFix::Automation): one row per switch, a Bootstrap switch
  (Switch::ToggleFormComponent, POST automation/switch) with its state badge. Locals: return_to ('dashboard' or
  'season_board'). Shown in the dashboard system column and on the Season board header; the stable id
  ('automation-switches-<return_to>') is the target of the turbo-stream answer of AutomationController#switch, which
  replaces both panels (and the board badge). Every toggle writes an 'automation.switched' event.
  The switch shows the stored value (an unreadable one counts as off); with ADMIN2_AUTOMATION=0 every switch is shown
  off and disabled, without the ops DB they are disabled too (the reason is the tooltip).
:ruby
  env_off = DataFix::Automation.env_off?
  ops_ready = Ops.available?
  state_css = { 'on' => 'text-bg-success', 'paused' => 'text-bg-warning', 'off' => 'text-bg-secondary' }
  disabled_reason = t('pipeline_automation.switches.ops_unavailable') unless ops_ready
  disabled_reason = t('pipeline_automation.switches.env_off', key: DataFix::Automation::ENV_KEY) if env_off
.automation-switches{ id: "automation-switches-#{return_to}" }
  - if env_off
    .alert.alert-warning.small.py-1.px-2.mb-2{ data: { automation_env_off: 'true' } }= disabled_reason
  - elsif !ops_ready
    .alert.alert-secondary.small.py-1.px-2.mb-2= disabled_reason
  %ul.list-unstyled.mb-0
    - DataFix::Automation.switches.each do |switch|
      - state = switch.state
      %li.d-flex.align-items-center.gap-2.py-1{ data: { automation_switch: switch.key, automation_state: state } }
        = render(Switch::ToggleFormComponent.new(url: automation_switch_path, name: 'value', checked: !env_off && switch.stored,
                                                 label: t("pipeline_automation.switches.#{switch.key}.label"),
                                                 id: "automation-switch-#{return_to}-#{switch.key}",
                                                 params: { switch: switch.key, return_to: },
                                                 disabled: disabled_reason.present?, reason: disabled_reason,
                                                 help: t("pipeline_automation.switches.#{switch.key}.help"),
                                                 form_class: 'flex-grow-1', label_class: 'small'))
        %span.badge{ class: state_css[state] }
          = t("pipeline_automation.switches.states.#{state}")
